WEBVTT

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:28.150
Okay. Right here.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:30.400
Be quiet!

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.830
You be quiet, Sachi!

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.400
You're making the most noise! Keep it down!

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.370
Hey!

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.910
Yeah. Okay, okay, around here should do it.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.810
We'll nail it in later.

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:47.000
The old man will get angry if we wake him up.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.100
He'll be so happy to see this.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.290
We'll get more donations with this.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:59.890
How about starting today by going door-to-door asking for donations for a trip to Nogiku Island?

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:03.910
Hey, that was my idea, so you better remember that!

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:05.100
It was mine!

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.540
I know, I know.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:09.620
I'll tell Bro Joe once he comes back.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.400
Oh me, oh my!

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:16.180
Come over here! The door's locked.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.190
The old man isn't inside sleeping?

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:25.380
That old man, where could <i>he</i> be so early in the morning?

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.210
He tricked us and slipped away!

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.220
Wh-Where to?

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:34.880
Where else!? To see Bro Joe!

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:45.270
The children are probably upset right now.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:47.130
Probably...

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:53.560
But since this is my job now, I should keep it separate from my private life.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:57.940
My duty is to be a boxing coach now.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.810
That's thanks to you, Miss.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:05.660
Once again, thank you for all you've done.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:09.830
It's because of the desperate fight between Rikiishi-kun and Yabuki-kun

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:14.750
which taught the inmates to box.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:21.400
I have done nothing in comparison.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:23.430
Joe!

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.430
Wait for me, Joe!

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:31.030
Starting today, I'll pound boxing into you with everything I have.

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:33.620
But you need to know and remember:

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:38.400
For the Sake of Tomorrow #4 and #5 will be difficult at first.

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:03.300
You won't be given much time for boxing practice. Hey, everyone, hurry up. Hurry!

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:08.310
They've got it easy since all they have to do is yell.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:10.690
Don't complain. Don't complain.

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:14.270
Let's just finish this up so we can have some fun boxing.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:16.690
You're right. You're right.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.270
All right, let's do this!

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.670
Take a look at this, Miss.

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:27.960
What do you think?

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:30.560
They've never worked this hard.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:37.460
Your boxing idea has definitely been a positive influence on the prison.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:41.720
I'm also grateful that you brought a coach along with you.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:47.310
We will do everything in our power to make Danpei-shi...

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:50.760
H-Huh? Where did Danpei-san go?

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:00.270
Sorry to interrupt your work, but do you know Joe? Yabuki Joe.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.020
Yabuki? I'm not sure.

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.850
I don't have time for him.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:05.930
All right. Step aside!

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.610
Hey, old man!

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.950
Oh, Nishi-kun!

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:14.960
Don't worry about Joe. He's doing well!

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.460
Well, that's what I'd like to say...

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:19.460
What happened?

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:22.960
Take a look over there. Look!

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:40.500
What? What's he up to?

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:43.950
Joe has been this way lately.

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:48.360
He sometimes digs up the potatoes using his bare hands instead of a shovel.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:52.920
I don't know what he's thinking, but it seems like he wants to break his bones.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:56.310
Joe changed after the fight with Rikiishi.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:58.790
Even the look in his eyes has changed.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:02.320
Do you know if there's a reason behind this?

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:05.300
Perhaps this is...

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:10.550
This is getting interesting!

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:15.890
That damn Joe. He's starting to hone his skills.

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:21.100
Joe!

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:25.110
Hey, old man! Long time no see!

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.630
How is everything? Doing okay?

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:30.320
I'm full of energy, as you can see.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:35.380
That aside, old man, the boxing tournament is only ten days away.

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:36.600
You know what that means, right?

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:41.290
Yeah, I just heard that from the warden.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.970
You wait and see, old man.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:47.260
This time, you won't see Rikiishi and me have a double KO.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:51.160
I see. I see what you mean.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:55.310
You're training for the tournament by hoeing with one hand.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:58.830
You're training your wrist strength, right?

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:00.640
That's right, eh?

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:03.670
Joe, that's it, right?

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:12.780
My match with Rikiishi reminded me that the snap is a basic principle of boxing.

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:18.790
In that match, he twisted his fist once each punch connected.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:20.590
A twist punch.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:22.000
That's the key.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:24.290
I see now.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:35.520
And now that I understand that, there's no way I won't use it.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:36.850
I'll make it mine.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:49.480
I see!

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:50.750
I knew it!

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:54.570
In the middle of his fight with Rikiishi,

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:57.250
he learned what I was about to teach him.

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:02.250
But you know, old man, I don't think I can defeat Rikiishi with this training alone.

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:06.210
I need something else, for sure. Another key...

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:12.780
I've been waiting for you, old man!

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:16.090
Every day. Every single day! Every day you didn't come, I waited for the next day!

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:19.100
In all honesty, I was starting to get frustrated.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.910
Now, teach me, old man!

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:26.680
Teach me For the Sake of Tomorrow #4, #5, and #6. All of it!

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.110
This time I will definitely defeat that Rikiishi bastard!

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:33.650
Wh-What? What is it?

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:39.280
Guards, the siren is sounding! The siren!

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:41.990
The siren is right on time.

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:44.110
All right, farm work is done for today!

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:46.290
You now have some free time!

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.790
Yay!

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.090
It's first come, first serve!

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:52.520
I'm first!

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:53.480
I'm second!

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:54.590
And I'm third!

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:59.640
Hey, hey, hey, how long are you going to hug the sandbag for?

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:00.720
Hurry up and get started!

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:08.230
There's a pair left!

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:13.460
Well, well, if it isn't Aoyama.

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:15.770
Listen, this isn't for kids. You'll just get beaten up.

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:16.610
You better stop while you can!

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:22.940
No fair! I found those gloves first!

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:24.180
Please give them back to me.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.720
So what?

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:29.210
If you want them, come and get them, you weakling!

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.910
I'd gladly take you on any day.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:33.360
Later!

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:39.370
Hey! Get off already, I want my turn!

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:49.130
He did it! Way to go, Arai!

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:52.420
Three more matches and you'll be the champion of cell block four!

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:54.820
Way to go, Arai! Do your best!

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:06.940
Old man, work time is over now.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:11.620
Hurry up and teach me For the Sake of Tomorrow #4.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:13.090
Hey!

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:18.210
Joe, I'm now the coach for everyone here.

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:21.750
I'm sorry, but I can't devote all my time to you anymore.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:23.050
What?

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:26.050
N-No way! What are you saying!?

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.920
I came here to coach the inmates.

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:33.200
Well, you carry on with your single-handed digging.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.520
Wait a minute, old man!

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:38.110
Even with so little time before the tournament, you won't coach me?

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:41.070
I'm saying I don't need to.

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:47.660
For the Sake of Tomorrow #4 relates to wrist strengthening, which you're already doing.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:52.730
I was going to teach you how to make your snap stronger.

00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:56.170
That's why there's nothing for me to teach you right now.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:11:03.090
If you really want me to coach you, get back to your single-handed digging.

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:07.620
Dig all the way over to that fence.

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:12.430
Old man, are you pulling my leg?

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:15.730
If you are, I can't trust you anymore.

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.030
I see.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:21.630
So what you're saying is that you don't trust your coach.

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:22.730
Fine, don't do it.

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:27.180
Let me make it clear that I won't help you until you reach that fence.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:31.150
I'll consider coaching you if you get there.

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:32.500
Well then, off I go.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:44.840
D-Damn it, that shitty old man!

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:49.090
After bowing down and asking for help,

00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:50.140
what the hell was that attitude!?

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:53.710
Wait and see, I'll show you that I'll do it!

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:57.770
Damn it!

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:06.450
I don't...

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:07.880
I don't understand.

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:11.610
I've never seen the old man be so cold.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:14.830
There must be something going on. There must be!

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:21.540
This is a little tough. Don't do it so fast.

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:26.390
Oh geez!

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:28.310
What's with this pathetic bunch!?

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:30.550
This is just a warm-up!

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:34.930
If this tires you out, then there's a long way to go before you can put on some gloves!

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:44.940
Rikiishi-san!

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:51.770
I've never had a chance to see Rikiishi-san hit the sandbag before!

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:53.640
I'll definitely take this opportunity to watch.

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:14.410
Awesome!

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:16.050
This is unreal!

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.770
Wow! His sounds are on a different level!

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:27.440
Rikiishi-san, this time you'll take that Yabuki bastard down easily, right?

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:29.700
That lucky draw won't happen again, right?

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:33.660
Yeah, that won't happen again.

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:35.690
Yeah. Yeah!

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:41.490
This time, really crush him into bits and pieces...

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:43.220
That's not it.

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:46.670
This is not a fight. This time I will box. Box, not fight!

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:51.840
What do you mean!? Rikiishi-san, you don't hate Yabuki anymore?

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:53.680
You guys really don't get it.

00:13:57.540 --> 00:14:00.750
The reason that match ended in a draw

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:03.690
is because I was full of hatred!

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:06.570
What goes on in a boxing ring is not a fight!

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:11.570
In the boxing ring, there should only be refined, calm, honed techniques present!

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:13.540
Boxing is an art form!

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.430
You must defeat your opponent as fast as possible, calmly and precisely.

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:20.710
You must become a perfect fighting machine. That's what boxing is all about!

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:23.070
But right now, my fighting spirit is different.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:29.150
It isn't the same as when I fought Joe.

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:32.950
Right now, my fighting spirit is exploding from the bottom of my heart!

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:44.910
As expected of Rikiishi.

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:49.950
He grasped an important concept amidst that bloody battle!

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:52.580
He'll become even stronger now!

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:55.370
It'll take more than just willpower to beat him next time.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:04.080
Now, more than ever, I need to teach For the Sake of Tomorrow #5 to Joe.

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:13.810
But Joe, For the Sake of Tomorrow #5 is going to be tough.

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:14.850
It's going to be ruthless!

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:18.300
Don't you dare lose, Joe!

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:36.270
He's gone nuts after watching Rikiishi-san train!

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:40.440
He did it again!

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:42.140
I feel like I'm going to explode from laughing!

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:44.120
What are you guys doing here?

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:46.370
Stop fooling around and get back to your practice!

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.290
All right!

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:52.970
Damn! Damn, damn, damn...

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:56.520
Damn, damn!

00:15:58.350 --> 00:15:59.550
Aoyama-kun.

00:16:01.590 --> 00:16:03.690
You're quite enthusiastic.

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:05.560
Do you really like boxing that much?

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:08.790
I love it.

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:10.070
I absolutely love it!

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.340
Is that so?

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:15.780
But your body is a bit small for fighting...

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:17.320
Fighting?

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:20.600
No! Boxing isn't fighting!

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:24.000
They both involve punches, but they're different.

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:25.890
You can't be angry when you box!

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:29.960
That's what I believe.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:31.670
And? So what?

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:37.760
That's why... That's why I believe I can be a boxer, even though I can't fight very well.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:41.310
I-If I'm wrong, then sorry. I apologize.

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:45.940
What do you think? Would you like to give it a try?

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:52.230
I'm saying I'll coach you because you seem to have some talent.

00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:54.400
What do you think? Do you want to give it a try?

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:56.410
R-Really?

00:16:56.410 --> 00:17:00.190
Yup. As long as you can dedicate yourself.

00:17:21.780 --> 00:17:23.510
Just you wait, old man.

00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:30.110
Just a little bit longer, damn it.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:02.640
Joe!

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:05.430
Joe!

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:08.410
Joe, what happened?

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:09.470
Are you okay?

00:18:12.460 --> 00:18:13.610
I finally did it!

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:16.610
Nishi, you saw that, didn't you?

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:19.150
Yeah! I saw it.

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:22.000
You really did it, Joe!

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:27.580
With this done, the old man should have no problem.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:30.510
The old man, huh...

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:33.630
What? What's wrong?

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:38.370
Well, you see, he's coaching a weird guy right now,

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:43.020
and he ignored me when I told him you were almost done.

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:43.600
Weird guy?

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:49.640
What? Who's this weird guy?

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:53.180
That Aoyama guy.

00:18:53.180 --> 00:18:58.150
The old man sure has an odd taste; there's no need to take him so seriously.

00:18:58.640 --> 00:18:59.650
Aoyama?

00:19:03.970 --> 00:19:06.230
I don't care whether it's "Aoyama" or "Akayama."

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:09.000
I guess the old man's just bored out of his mind without me.

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:11.170
Poor him.

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:15.890
Well then, I guess it's time to put the old man to work.

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:17.440
Later!

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:24.150
Regardless of how much you do what you want, I wonder if the old man will listen to you.

00:19:45.770 --> 00:19:47.970
Hey, hey, dear Yabuki!

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:50.580
Did you come to see Rikiishi-san's training too?

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:54.530
It's so cool! Rikiishi-san's boxing is an art!

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:58.460
Do you even know what art is!? You'd better start studying!

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:03.460
Quit laughing. What art are you talking about?

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:06.940
All I can see is a bunch of idiots in a row.

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:14.800
Well, I'll stop interrupting. Do your best.

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:17.250
One, two, one, two...

00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:21.580
No, no, that's wrong!

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.450
Your right should be right next to your chin.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:24.900
Right!

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:26.030
Now bring your left in front of you!

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:26.820
Right!

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:32.310
Yeah, that's it. Now, bring your chin down a bit more.

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:32.710
Right!

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:35.210
Yeah, but with speed. Speed!

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:36.820
Right!

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:39.140
Now it's looking much better!

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:43.660
Keep it up!

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:44.180
R-Right!

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:49.930
Yes, that's it. Don't forget how to do it.

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:50.700
Hey, old man!

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:53.680
Yabuki-san!

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:56.210
I finished the single-handed digging.

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:57.690
I'm completely finished.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:04.200
So now, like you promised, hurry up and start coaching me.

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:06.230
What are you doing?

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:08.200
Practice! Carry on with your practice!

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.030
Right!

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:12.940
No, that's wrong!

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:15.540
Keep your elbows tucked in at your sides!

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:16.170
Old man!

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:20.640
Whenever you attack or defend, you'll need to use those muscles.

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:21.670
Got it?

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:22.300
Yes!

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:25.240
Hey, old man, stop irritating people!

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:28.820
The tournament is coming up. I don't have any time to waste!

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:30.310
I'm begging you, old man!

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:33.670
It's getting annoyingly noisy here!

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:36.250
Old man!

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:39.410
Just when I thought we had found a secluded place...

00:21:39.410 --> 00:21:41.900
Aoyama-kun, let's go somewhere else.

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:44.240
I still have much to teach you.

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:46.380
You're really learning quickly.

00:21:46.380 --> 00:21:48.100
I have things to teach you.

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:49.660
Come on!

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:52.710
Hold it. Hold it right there, old man!

00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:54.860
Listen to me.

00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:57.620
I'm not kidding around.

00:21:57.620 --> 00:22:01.210
I'm not confident that I can beat Rikiishi,

00:22:01.940 --> 00:22:04.480
but I will still do whatever it takes to win.

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:05.260
Do you understand me?

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:08.280
I truly need your help in so many ways.

00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:11.180
I even finished the single-handed digging you told me to do.

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:12.350
Why are you being so condescending?

00:22:12.350 --> 00:22:15.220
What happened? Eh, old man!?

00:22:19.220 --> 00:22:21.190
Aoyama-kun, are you hurt?

00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:23.630
No, not at all.

00:22:23.630 --> 00:22:25.600
I see. I'm relieved.

00:22:25.600 --> 00:22:27.040
Let's go!

00:22:27.040 --> 00:22:28.350
Hurry up.

00:22:28.350 --> 00:22:29.380
R-Right!

00:22:31.070 --> 00:22:32.970
Are you okay with this?

00:22:32.970 --> 00:22:34.740
Yabuki-kun is glaring at me!

00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:37.820
What are you saying? There's nothing to worry about.

00:22:37.820 --> 00:22:42.170
If you do my secret training, you won't need to fear him.

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:43.000
But... Me?

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:44.260
Don't worry, don't worry!

00:22:44.260 --> 00:22:45.750
He won't be afraid...?

00:22:55.120 --> 00:22:59.290
You'll see, your strength will be way beyond his.

00:23:00.410 --> 00:23:02.710
I'll prove it to you myself.

00:23:03.730 --> 00:23:05.720
Is that really so?

00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:09.590
I wonder...

00:23:09.590 --> 00:23:11.780
You'll understand in time.

00:23:11.780 --> 00:23:14.360
He won't be a problem at all.

00:23:14.360 --> 00:23:16.000
Don't worry about him!

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:24.040
Why?

00:23:24.040 --> 00:23:25.770
What's wrong?

00:23:25.770 --> 00:23:27.220
What happened?

00:23:28.360 --> 00:23:29.540
Old man!

00:24:40.160 --> 00:24:43.080
Holding back my tears, I gave Joe the cold shoulder.

00:24:44.080 --> 00:24:47.480
Under the heavy rain, Joe reflects in solitude.

00:24:47.480 --> 00:24:48.590
Joe!

00:24:48.590 --> 00:24:51.090
Persevere through the isolation and fly toward tomorrow!

00:24:51.090 --> 00:24:55.940
Now, for Joe, who's been given a bitter trial, which way is tomorrow!?
